  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when recent history shows volatility or mixed sentiment; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10%.",
    "When sentiment is low (near 0) but price action is volatile, the model fails to capture mean reversion and predicts a smooth linear increase instead of a jagged path.",
    "Forecasts show significant lag in reacting to sudden price spikes; the model underestimates volatility during high-sentiment periods and overestimates stability.",
    "In scenarios with alternating positive/negative sentiment, the model assumes monotonic growth while true outcomes exhibit sharp reversals (e.g., dropping 10-15 points before recovering).",
    "The 30-day horizon forecast is systematically too optimistic; actual outcomes often end lower than predicted unless a sustained high-sentiment trend (>0.4) exists for multiple consecutive days."
  ]
}
